<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6123" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căīcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căȳcus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
		111</span></i>), i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάικος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river of Greater Mysia</i>, <i>which
				takes its rise on Mt. Teuthras</i>, <i>passes near
				Pergamus</i>, <i>and flows into the sea opposite
				Lesbos;</i> now the <i>Bakhir Tchai</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 29, 72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 37,
				18, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 18, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30,
				32, § 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 4,
				370</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2, 243</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15, 278</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Luc.
				3, 203</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the companions of Æneas</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1,
				183</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 35</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
